Player: This Atomon looks different from the Iron Atomon.

Player: It doesn't seem to keep one fixed shape.

Player: Its form can change depending on the space around it.

Player: But it doesn't seem to spread out and fill the entire space.

Player: It still seems to have a definite volume.

Player: So... it seems to have a definite volume, but not a definite shape.

Player: But what is the phase of this Mercury Atomon?

Player: <Empty Text Event>
- Solid
  Player: Not quite. A solid keeps both a definite shape and a definite volume. This Mercury Atomon does not keep a fixed shape.

- Liquid
  Player: Yes! Mercury is a liquid at normal room temperature. It has a definite volume, but it takes the shape of its container.

- Gas
  Not quite. A gas does not have a definite shape or volume and tends to spread out to fill the available space.

Player: Then the Mercury Atomon is a liquid.

Player: It has a definite volume, but its shape can change.

[signal arg="quest_notify:quest_chain_002_01:observe_mercury"]

Player: I think I'm starting to understand the difference between a solid and a liquid.